WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.207 --> 00:00:16.808
looked at the nomads, who seemed just as perplexed as the kids were.

2
00:00:16.828 --> 00:00:19.288
"What kind of insects are those?"

3
00:00:19.768 --> 00:00:20.849
he asked the nomads.

4
00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:22.009
"Are they dangerous?"

5
00:00:22.029 --> 00:00:26.230
"I've never seen such creatures before," one nomad responded.

6
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.671
"They aren't native to the Far Frontier."

7
00:00:29.471 --> 00:00:30.991
"Hey!" Darb pointed.

8
00:00:31.011 --> 00:00:32.732
"They all just disappeared!"

9
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:34.520
"That's weird."

10
00:00:35.341 --> 00:00:36.461
Zann felt uneasy.

11
00:00:36.481 --> 00:00:42.043
"What if those beetles are some kind of strange off-world creatures that Morb is using to guard his

12
00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:44.845
contraption? They might be more dangerous than they look."

13
00:00:45.585 --> 00:00:47.546
"Dangerous enough to scare off Wyssa?"

14
00:00:47.966 --> 00:00:49.166
Perda sounded skeptical.

15
00:00:49.186 --> 00:00:52.288
"She's not even scared of a scatter beast!"

16
00:00:53.188 --> 00:00:55.909
"Let's climb up there and see what happens," Darb said.

17
00:00:55.929 --> 00:00:59.110
"Maybe we can break the contraption apart without magic."

18
00:00:59.131 --> 00:01:03.961
"We'll stand guard and alert you if Morb is approaching," one of the nomads said.

19
00:01:03.981 --> 00:01:10.065
"Okay." Zann could tell that the nomads wanted to stay far away from that contraption.

20
00:01:10.866 --> 00:01:11.627
He didn't blame them.

21
00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:15.549
Morb was awfully scary, and so were his contraptions.

22
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.593
But Zann knew that this could be their best chance to stop the evil villain's plans.

23
00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:25.337
Zann, Perda, and Darb climbed up to the top of the plateau.

24
00:01:26.077 --> 00:01:27.598
Zann walked toward the contraption.

25
00:01:28.339 --> 00:01:33.223
But after just a few steps, he found his path blocked by an invisible wall of energy.

26
00:01:33.243 --> 00:01:36.045
"There's a Shield spell here," he said.

27
00:01:36.826 --> 00:01:37.466
Perda nodded.

28
00:01:37.486 --> 00:01:41.669
"We should have known that Morb wouldn't leave his contraption unguarded."

29
00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:43.551
Darb glanced around.

30
00:01:43.571 --> 00:01:46.093
"There's no sign of those beetles.

31
00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.935
Why would he need them if he has a Shield spell?"

32
00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.558
Perda shrugged and poked at the invisible shield.

33
00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:55.220
"Should we try to break through this?"

34
00:01:56.381 --> 00:01:57.702
"How?" Zann said.

35
00:01:57.722 --> 00:01:59.804
"Our magic barely works here.

36
00:02:00.512 --> 00:02:02.673
Besides, I'm sure Morb used a strong spell."

37
00:02:02.693 --> 00:02:05.854
"I bet that fireball would have broken through."

38
00:02:06.355 --> 00:02:07.035
Perda frowned.

39
00:02:07.055 --> 00:02:10.516
"I wonder what made Wyssa zap off like that."

40
00:02:10.536 --> 00:02:12.057
"Who knows?"

41
00:02:12.857 --> 00:02:15.318
Darb started walking toward the edge of the plateau.

42
00:02:15.338 --> 00:02:19.300
"But come on, we should get out of here before Morb comes back."

43
00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.601
Zann had to agree with that.

44
00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:25.322
They climbed back down and told the nomads about the Shield spell.

45
00:02:25.342 --> 00:02:27.163
"Is your friend coming back?"

46
00:02:27.683 --> 00:02:28.764
one of the nomads asked.

47
00:02:29.724 --> 00:02:30.444
"You mean Wyssa?"

48
00:02:31.004 --> 00:02:31.865
Zann shook his head.

49
00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.145
"I don't know.

50
00:02:33.505 --> 00:02:34.986
Maybe we should try to contact her.

51
00:02:35.426 --> 00:02:36.666
Are there message moths out here?"

52
00:02:37.606 --> 00:02:39.227
"No," a nomad replied.

53
00:02:39.247 --> 00:02:41.367
"But we can send her a message."

54
00:02:42.468 --> 00:02:43.948
"How?" Darb asked.

55
00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:47.289
"A sound message," another nomad said.

56
00:02:47.309 --> 00:02:51.450
"We send sound waves through the air and the ground to form thoughts and feelings."

57
00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.411
Zann wasn't sure that Wyssa would understand that kind of message.

58
00:02:56.031 --> 00:03:01.105
But he didn't have any better ideas, so he stood back and watched while the nomads sent their

59
00:03:01.145 --> 00:03:07.307
message. They stomped their feet and danced in a circle, waving their arms and rubbing their hands together

60
00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:09.187
to form spurts of magic energy.

61
00:03:09.927 --> 00:03:14.209
Even the hoof beasts stopped grazing and watched the nomads with interest.

62
00:03:14.229 --> 00:03:17.470
"That magic is cool," Darb whispered.

63
00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.070
"I can feel it!"

64
00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:22.251
Zann could feel the nomads' magic message too.

65
00:03:22.971 --> 00:03:25.572
The nomads were saying, "Where are you?

66
00:03:26.292 --> 00:03:28.253
We wish you were here with us."

67
00:03:28.273 --> 00:03:35.719
"I hope Wyssa feels it and comes back soon," Perda said after the nomads finished sending the message.

68
00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:38.500
"We need her help to find Gliss."

69
00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:43.264
"Maybe we should split up and keep searching for both of them," Darb suggested.

70
00:03:43.284 --> 00:03:45.225
"We could cover more ground that way."

71
00:03:45.245 --> 00:03:48.667
"No, you might get lost," a nomad said.

72
00:03:48.687 --> 00:03:53.210
"In any case, people from our tribe are still searching for your friend Gliss.

73
00:03:53.591 --> 00:03:55.352
They will send a message when they find her."

74
00:03:56.076 --> 00:03:59.778
The hoof beasts had gone back to grazing after the message had been sent.

75
00:04:00.518 --> 00:04:03.440
But suddenly one of them let out a sharp whistle.

76
00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.462
The other hoof beasts abruptly raised their heads.

77
00:04:07.222 --> 00:04:10.324
Their ears swiveled around, and their nostrils flared.

78
00:04:11.044 --> 00:04:13.526
Then they all took off at a gallop.

79
00:04:13.546 --> 00:04:16.007
"Hey! Where are they going?"

80
00:04:16.547 --> 00:04:17.548
a nomad exclaimed.

81
00:04:18.348 --> 00:04:19.889
Another nomad whistled sharply.

82
00:04:20.549 --> 00:04:22.370
But the hoof beasts ignored the sound.

83
00:04:23.051 --> 00:04:25.212
They soon disappeared over the horizon.

84
00:04:25.992 --> 00:04:26.892
"That was strange."

85
00:04:27.372 --> 00:04:28.353
One nomad frowned.

86
00:04:28.373 --> 00:04:29.973
"What frightened them?"

87
00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:32.614
"Look!" Darb pointed.

88
00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:34.014
"Here comes Wyssa!"

89
00:04:34.775 --> 00:04:35.275
"Oh, good!"

90
00:04:35.595 --> 00:04:36.155
Zann said.

91
00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:41.416
"Maybe she startled the hoof beasts," Perda said.

92
00:04:42.317 --> 00:04:44.037
Zann opened his mouth to respond.

93
00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:50.899
Instead he gasped as a Red Share struck him so strongly that he staggered and almost fell.

94
00:04:51.639 --> 00:04:54.260
It was from Gliss, and she was still terrified!

95
00:04:55.008 --> 00:04:56.669
The others didn't notice his reaction.

96
00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:58.911
They were hurrying to meet Wyssa.

97
00:05:00.232 --> 00:05:03.754
Zann staggered after them, his head throbbing with the Share.

98
00:05:03.774 --> 00:05:06.596
"Why did you zap off like that?"

99
00:05:07.017 --> 00:05:07.957
Perda asked Wyssa.

100
00:05:07.977 --> 00:05:11.380
"You were about to destroy Morb's contraption!"

101
00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.701
"Was it the insects?"

102
00:05:14.162 --> 00:05:14.762
Darb asked.

103
00:05:15.603 --> 00:05:22.628
"They looked harmless, but maybe—" "They are harmless," Wyssa said with a short laugh.

104
00:05:23.348 --> 00:05:25.910
"I apologize for being such a coward earlier.

105
00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.132
After all, what kind of fool is afraid of a few silly blank bugs?

106
00:05:30.992 --> 00:05:32.853
I must have been losing my mind!"

107
00:05:32.873 --> 00:05:34.715
"Blank bugs?"

108
00:05:35.075 --> 00:05:36.235
Darb said with interest.

109
00:05:37.076 --> 00:05:42.579
The Share was still distracting Zann, but he also couldn't help noticing that Wyssa was acting oddly.

110
00:05:43.319 --> 00:05:48.562
She wasn't the type of person to apologize for anything or to call herself a coward.

111
00:05:48.582 --> 00:05:50.203
"Are you okay?"

112
00:05:50.744 --> 00:05:54.561
he asked, doing his best to ignore Gliss' terror for the moment.

113
00:05:54.581 --> 00:05:58.102
"Good question," Wyssa said with a smirk.

114
00:05:58.922 --> 00:06:00.843
"Actually, I'm better than ever.

115
00:06:01.443 --> 00:06:02.143
Much better."

116
00:06:02.983 --> 00:06:03.723
Perda blinked.

117
00:06:04.424 --> 00:06:05.304
"What do you mean?"

118
00:06:06.964 --> 00:06:09.085
Wyssa let out a wild cackle.

119
00:06:09.845 --> 00:06:12.366
Suddenly there was an evil glimmer in her eye.

120
00:06:12.386 --> 00:06:16.387
"I thought you children were supposed to be clever!

121
00:06:16.887 --> 00:06:19.828
And yet you're always so easy to trick!"

122
00:06:20.576 --> 00:06:24.420
Before Zann could figure out what that meant, Wyssa snapped her fingers.

123
00:06:25.121 --> 00:06:28.544
Her face and body shimmered and started to change.

124
00:06:29.405 --> 00:06:33.409
A shiver ran down Zann's spine as a new face took shape.

125
00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:35.532
Zann gasped.

126
00:06:37.093 --> 00:06:37.614
"Morb!"
